Hi 

I would like my machine to boot the OS automatically and have been  
trying, unsuccessfully, to get the SRM to use the 0 option from the 
aboot configuration list.

Below are the current SRM variables and boot configuration. 
boot_flags doesn't appear to persist between power-downs although I 
thought it was a system variable from what I've read on the SRM 
howto.

I had hoped that by setting boot_flags to 0 it would use the 0 option 
from my aboot list. 

At the moment it goes directly to the aboot prompt and I have to 
select my config choice. 

There is a message about an "unzip :unknown compression method" but 
the list archives seem to suggest I can ignore this error.

Is there a way to get the SRM to tell aboot to use the first listed 
configuration? 

Thanx in advance.
Dp.

aboot version 0.9b
==================
auto_action	boot
bootdef_dev	dka0
boot_file		2/vmlinuz
boot_flags		0

file=2/vmlinuz
root=/dev/sda3
initrd=/initrd.img
==================




